{
  "id": "equivariant_sheaves.induction_data_reverse",
  "title": "Reverse-direction induction: reconstructing X as G ×^P S from a QFD",
  "kind": "proposition",
  "status": "staged",
  "href": "equivariant_sheaves/equivariant_sheaves_induction_data_reverse.html",
  "primary_topic": "equivariant_sheaves",
  "topics": [
    "equivariant_sheaves"
  ],
  "body_html": "<h1>Reverse-direction induction</h1>\n<p>The paper's Proposition 2.8 goes <strong>forward</strong>: given <code>InductionDatum d</code>\non $X'$, the induced complex $X := G \\times^P X'$ is a $G$-cell complex\nwith $X'$ as a QFD.</p>\n<p>At the abstract cell-poset level this admits a <strong>converse</strong>: given a\nQFD $S \\subseteq X$ with subgroup $G'$, plus a cosheaf-of-subgroups\n$P$ satisfying four axioms below, one can reconstruct $X \\simeq\nG \\times^P S$.</p>\n<h2>Data</h2>\n<p>Fix <code>IsQuasiFundDomain G' S</code> on $X$.  A choice of <strong>induction data</strong>\nconsists of $P : X \\to \\mathrm{Subgroup}(G)$ (defined on $S$) satisfying:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>(P0)</strong> Cosheaf monotonicity on $S$:\n  $E \\le F \\Rightarrow P_F \\le P_E$.</li>\n<li><strong>(P1)</strong> $G'$-conjugation equivariance:\n  $n \\in G' \\Rightarrow P_{n \\cdot E} = n P_E n^{-1}$.</li>\n<li><strong>(P3)</strong> Well-definedness upper bound:\n  $P_E \\subseteq \\mathrm{Fix}_G(E) = \\mathrm{MulAction.stabilizer}\\, G\\, E$.\n  This is what makes the natural map $[(g, E)] \\mapsto g \\cdot E$\n  well-defined on the induction quotient.</li>\n<li><strong>(P4)</strong> Fix factorisation:\n  $\\mathrm{Fix}_G(E) = \\mathrm{Fix}_{G'}(E) \\cdot P_E$.  This is what\n  makes the natural map <strong>injective</strong>: the QFD's orbit witness\n  $g^{-1} h n \\in \\mathrm{Fix}_G(E)$ can be absorbed via (P4) as\n  $u \\cdot p$, letting us adjust the $G'$ witness to $n u^{-1}$ and\n  the residual lands in $P_E$.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The paper's original (P2) axiom $P_E \\cap G' \\subseteq\n\\mathrm{Fix}_{G'}(E)$ is a derived lemma from (P3).</p>\n<p><strong>Setwise vs pointwise.</strong> The canonical <em>setwise</em> choice\n$P_E := \\mathrm{MulAction.stabilizer}\\, G\\, E$ satisfies (P1), (P3),\n(P4) but generally <strong>fails (P0)</strong> — the setwise stabiliser of a\nhigher-dim cell need not fix its lower-dim faces.  The paper's\ngeometric setting uses the <em>pointwise</em> fixator, which does satisfy\n(P0) by continuity.  At the abstract cell-poset level (P0) must be\nsupplied as external data.</p>\n<h2>The reconstruction</h2>\n<p>Given <code>InductionData d</code> on <code>IsQuasiFundDomain G' S</code>, define the\nequivalence</p>\n<p>$$(g, E) \\sim (h, F) \\ :\\iff\\ \\exists n \\in G',\\\n    n \\cdot E = F \\wedge g^{-1} h n \\in P_E$$</p>\n<p>on $G \\times S.\\mathrm{carrier}$, and set</p>\n<p>$$Q_d \\;:=\\; (G \\times S.\\mathrm{carrier}) / \\sim.$$</p>\n<p>The natural map $[(g, E)] \\mapsto g \\cdot E$ is:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>well-defined by (P3);</li>\n<li>surjective by the QFD's <code>surj</code> axiom;</li>\n<li>injective by the sharpened orbit lemma\n  $g \\cdot E = h \\cdot F \\ \\iff\\ \\exists n \\in G', n \\cdot E = F\n  \\wedge g^{-1} h n \\in P_E$\n  (proved via QFD <code>orbit_iff</code> + (P4)).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Together these give a <strong>$G$-equivariant bijection</strong></p>\n<p>$$\\mathrm{equivX} : Q_d \\ \\xrightarrow{\\ \\sim\\ }\\ X.$$</p>\n<h2>Face relation</h2>\n<p>The (←) direction of the face-relation characterisation</p>\n<p>$$\\Bigl(\\exists n \\in G',\\ n \\cdot E \\le F,\\ g_1^{-1} g_2 n \\in P_E\\Bigr)\n   \\ \\Longrightarrow\\ g_1 \\cdot E \\le g_2 \\cdot F$$</p>\n<p>follows from (P3) plus $G$-equivariance of $\\le$ on a <code>GCellComplex</code>.\nThe (→) converse is <em>not</em> provable at the abstract level; the paper\nrecovers it topologically through the CW structure.</p>\n<h2>Design note</h2>\n<p>At the paper level this is implicit in Proposition 2.8's uniqueness\nclaim (\"any CW structure on $X$ for which $\\iota$ is cellular and the\naction is cellular must have the same cell set\").  As a Lean theorem\nit is separated out because reconstruction is genuine content when\none starts from an abstract QFD without a pre-existing induction.</p>",
